# The implicit-`it` closure parameter was REMOVED from the surface. A program
# that still spells `xs.map(it * 2)` must be rejected with the teaching error
# that names the retirement and shows the replacement — never accepted, and
# never met with the edit-distance suggestion (`it`/`xs` is distance 2, so the
# generic path would answer "did you mean `xs`?", which is worse than useless).
#
# The rejection is a single spanned `E_UndefinedName` on the `it` token: after
# the removal `it` is an ordinary identifier, so this is exactly the diagnostic
# any other undefined name gets, plus the retirement note that displaces the
# suggestion.
#
# The fixture lives in its own directory (like break_value_removed_error/) so
# the rejected source stays OUT of the top-level fixture sweeps (fmt_idempotent,
# *_comparison, runtime_diff). Negative fixture: `gg check` must fail.
void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[int] ys = xs.map(it * 2)
    print(ys.len())
